#
# The LLVM major version of the clang-format and clang-tidy that check this tree. .clang-tidy
# enables check groups such as readability-*, and each LLVM major release adds checks to those
# groups. The CI format and clang-tidy steps, .githooks/pre-commit and the clang-format target
# require this version.
#
# The CI clang-tidy step holds the changed lines of a pull request to every enabled check, and the
# tree keeps the findings of earlier lines. A raise of the version therefore requires a review of
# each check that the new release adds to the enabled groups:
# 1. Compare `clang-tidy --list-checks` of the old and the new release. The difference lists the
#    added checks.
# 2. Run each added check over the tree with
#    `run-clang-tidy -p build -quiet -checks='-*,<check>' '/marupop/(src|tests|tools)/'`.
#    The output lists its findings.
# 3. Disable in .clang-tidy each added check whose findings contradict .clang-format or the style
#    of the tree.
23
